-- §4 `gen-sig` side condition `Q_sig ⊩ P'ᵢ` where the inferred `P'ᵢ` arrives as a
-- `requires` RESIDUAL and `Q_sig` is EMPTY.  Issue 1549, the signatured cell.
--
-- HAND-DERIVED FROM THE SPEC:
--   The body poses `Tag (Wrap t)`; §3 `inst` reduces it through
--   `impl Tag (Wrap a) requires Tag a` to the residual `Tag t`, and `t` is the
--   signature's own quantified variable.  The declared context is empty, and
--   ∅ ⊮ `Tag a`, so §4 `gen-sig` REJECTS at the definition site -- "a signature
--   is a contract the body must satisfy, not a floor it can raise".  It is never
--   silently widened to `Q_sig ∪ P'ᵢ`.
-- EXPECTED: reject at the DEFINITION, T-MISSING-CONSTRAINT
--   ("Could not deduce 'Tag a' from the signature of 'nest'").
--
-- BEFORE THE FIX this file was ACCEPTED at exit 0 by all three verbs, `run`
-- printed the correct `wrap(int)`, and the built binary SEGFAULTED -- the
-- coverage check never saw the residual either, because it reads the same
-- inferred-obligation projection.
--
-- ⚠️ DISTINCT FROM `s4-gen-sig-body-needs-more-rejected.mdk`, which pins the same
-- clause for a predicate the body infers DIRECTLY.  This one only becomes visible
-- once the recorded predicate is REDUCED; a checker that tested the recorded
-- `Tag (Wrap a)` against the declared set would find no bare-tyvar argument at
-- all and stay silent.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

interface Tag t where
  tagOf : t -> String

impl Tag Int where
  tagOf _ = "int"

impl Tag (Wrap a) requires Tag a where
  tagOf (Wrap x) = "wrap(\{tagOf x})"

nest : a -> String
nest x = tagOf (Wrap x)

main = println (nest 5)
